<title>ITALY: FORECAST-Italy seen issuing 39.5 trln lire BOT, CTZ.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Italy seen issuing 39.5 trln lire BOT, CTZ.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is seen issuing between 38.75 and 41.25 trillion lire of short term BOT bills and zero coupon certificates (CTZ) at auction on April 22, against 45.25 trillion lire maturing, a Reuter poll showed.</p>
<p>Analysts said the Treasury will continue to issue less BOTs than those maturing and might increase the CTZ offer given the fact that some 8.5 trillion lire of zero coupon certificates fall due at the end of April.</p>
<p>Settlement for the paper is on April 28.</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trillion of lire):</p>
<p>		    3Mo Bot  6Mo Bot 12Mo Bot 18Mo Ctz 24Mo CTz TOT</p>
<p>Banca di Roma    10.25    13.0     12.0    2.0	 4.0   41.25</p>
<p>Bank of America  10.00    12.5     11.0    2.0	 4.0   39.50</p>
<p>Caboto	     10.00    12.0     11.5    2.5	 3.5   39.50</p>
<p>BCI		  10.25    12.5     11.5    2.0	 2.5   38.75</p>
<p>Credito Italiano 10.00    12.5     11.5    2.0	 4.0   40.00</p>
<p>Indosuez	   10.00    12.75    12.0    2.0	 2.5   39.25</p>
<p>Prometeia	  10.00    12.0     11.5	  *10.00</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>Consensus	  10.0     12.5     11.5    2.0	 3.5   39.50</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>Maturing	   10.75    13.5     12.5	-	 8.5   45.25</p>
<p>*Refers to total CTZ issues for the entire month of April</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
</text>
